  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HJPC Judicial and prosecutorial efficiency Phase 2 - Special conditions grant agreement Domstolsverket</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">HJPC Judicial and prosecutorial efficiency Phase 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving Court Efficiency and Accountability of Judges and Prosecutors in BiH Phase 2</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Projektet &#xE4;r en forts&#xE4;ttning p&#xE5; f&#xF6;rb&#xE4;ttrad effektivisering inom HJPC.
Resultaten i den andra fasen &#xE4;r att f&#xF6;rb&#xE4;ttra effektiviteten i domstolar.
Effekten av st&#xF6;det &#xE4;r att ha ett domstolsystem som garanterar m&#xE4;nniskor r&#xE4;ttigheten till r&#xE4;ttvisa r&#xE4;tteg&#xE5;ngar inom rimlig tid. Detta &#xE4;r en f&#xF6;ruts&#xE4;ttning f&#xF6;r anslutning till EU-medlemskap. 
Effekterna av projektet kommer ocks&#xE5; bidra till att allm&#xE4;nhetens uppfattning av domstolsystem f&#xF6;rb&#xE4;ttras och ocks&#xE5; leda till en mer funktionell ekonomi.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">There are several overall intended outcomes contributing the overall impact of improving the efficiency of judiciary in Bosnia Herzegovina in the programme. They are as follows:-Improving court case management-Improving internal reorganization of courts and human resources at courts - Improving enforcement proceedings in judiciary-Improving gender equality, vulnerable groups and cooperation with NGOs- Reinforcing the Independence and Accountability of the Judiciary
Indicators have been developed for the following main outputs
Improved internal reorganization of courts to enable faster and better processing of tasks and work processes in courts in cooperation with SNCA Improved archive management at courts with the implementation the archive management and CMS records digitalisation process Increased number of processed cases, reduced lenght of proceedings and improved quality of proceedings in bankruptcy and liquidation casesImproved enforcement against movables, use of more efficient assets and means of enforcement and increased availability and visibility of information regarding public sale hearings Increased number of processed cases and reduced lenght of proceedings and influx of civi cases (against budget users) Increased number of processed, reduced the lenght of proceedings and improved quality of conducted of proceedings in bankruptcy and liquidation cases Improved promotion of court settlement and mediationPublic debate to identify the optimal system solution model for enforcement procedures is establishedImproved enforcement procedures by promoting and applying the Personal Data Protection Agency Opinion in order to obtain data on the property of a debtor Established and developed cooperation with the NGOs Improved work processes in enforcement departments and strengthened the role of court bailiffs and their training Established electronic system for submission, recording, processing and monitoring of judges and prosecutors&#x2019; financial statements - the SuRePro Monitor</narrative>
  </description>
